@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Option Desk - Snapshots, history and saved results

component "Permitted CSV / JSON\nor explicitly enabled provider" as input
component "Chain snapshot\nchain_*.json" as chain #C6E9C6
component "Far-expiry snapshot" as far
component "Greek ladder\ngreeks_*.json" as greeks
component "Positioning\nexposure_*.json" as exposure
component "Strategy plans\nstrategy_*.json" as plan
component "Comparison\ncomparison_*.json" as compare
component "Permitted underlying history" as history
component "Simulation\nsimulation_*.json" as sim
component "Backtest\nbacktest_*.json" as bt
component "Paper ledger\nforward_ledger.json" as forward
component "Local dashboard / readers" as dash
input --> chain
chain --> greeks
chain --> exposure
chain --> plan
far --> plan : two-expiry structures
plan --> compare
plan --> sim : terminal P/L distributions
history --> sim
history --> bt
plan --> forward : paper entry
chain --> forward : later mark
greeks --> dash
exposure --> dash
compare --> dash
sim --> dash
bt --> dash
forward --> dash
note bottom of chain
Provider IV may be solved or retained as a labelled fallback.
Imported IV stays user-supplied. Missing IV stays absent.
Missing inputs and degradation remain visible.
end note
note bottom of dash
Artifacts carry schema, time, versions and source metadata.
Replaced files are archived by default before atomic writes.
The dashboard reads artifacts. It does not create trades.
end note

caption Schemas: shell/src/optiondesk/contracts/. Simulation and backtests consume history, not a chain in place of history.
@enduml
